From f5402bc9beebe2ac8693018ddb7d13f537203671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Suresh, Prashanth" <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libva: Initialize the DRM file descriptor to -1

calloc() zero-initializes drm_state, leaving drm_state->fd at 0. If
device selection later fails before ever opening a real DRM fd (e.g.
va_DisplayContextConnect() finds no candidate device),
va_DisplayContextDestroy() unconditionally calls close(drm_state->fd),
closing fd 0 (typically stdin) -- a descriptor this driver doesn't
own. Initialize fd to -1 right after allocation so cleanup can never
close an unrelated descriptor; close(-1) is a safe EBADF no-op.

Tracked-On: NIACP3-1547
Signed-off-by: Suresh, Prashanth <prashanth.suresh@intel.com>
---
 va/android/va_android.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/va/android/va_android.cpp b/va/android/va_android.cpp
index b99f859..4a0286b 100644
--- a/va/android/va_android.cpp
+++ b/va/android/va_android.cpp
@@ -277,6 +277,7 @@ VADisplay vaGetDisplay(
         return NULL;
     }
 
+    drm_state->fd = -1;
     pDriverContext->drm_state = drm_state;
 
     return (VADisplay)pDisplayContext;
-- 
